-- title:
--   Right ideals of a maximal order arise from finite ideles
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $p$ be a prime, and consider the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}=\left(\frac{a,b}{\mathbb{Q}}\right)$. Assume `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b p`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit exactly when $p$ lies in the prime ideal attached to $v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ which is a maximal order, i.e. $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, $\Lambda$ spans $\mathbb{H}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, $\Lambda$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$, and every order containing $\Lambda$ equals $\Lambda$. Let $I$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ with $I\subseteq\Lambda$, stable under right multiplication by $\Lambda$ ($z\mu\in I$ for $z\in I$, $\mu\in\Lambda$), and of full rank in the sense that $n\Lambda\subseteq I$ for some nonzero integer $n$. Then there is a unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, the tensor product of $\mathbb{H}$ with the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $I=$ [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ x`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19): that is, $I$ is exactly the set of $z\in\mathbb{H}$ whose image $z\otimes 1$ lies in $x\cdot\widehat{\Lambda}$, where $\widehat{\Lambda}$ is the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele all of whose components are integral.
--
--   This is the classical local principality (equivalently, invertibility) of integral right ideals of a maximal order in a definite rational quaternion algebra ramified at a single prime, phrased adelically: every such ideal is cut out by a finite idele acting on the adelic completion of the order. It feeds the converse comparison [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_eq_ofFiniteIdele_of_forall_mul_mem`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_eq_ofFiniteIdele_of_forall_mul_mem), the membership criterion [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_units_forall_mem_iff_mem_ofFiniteIdele_of_forall_mul_mem`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_units_forall_mem_iff_mem_ofFiniteIdele_of_forall_mul_mem), and the identification of kernel ideals of an elliptic curve with ideals described by finite ideles.
